LGPL-3.0 subcomponent: libde265 (HEVC decoder)

This package is an adapter for the WebAssembly build of libde265, an open
H.265/HEVC decoder, distributed via the npm package @yume-chan/libde265
(https://github.com/yume-chan/libde265) and vendored for this project in
examples/basic/vendor/libde265-esm.js + libde265.wasm (sha256-pinned).

The libde265 binary artifact is licensed under the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 3.0 (LGPL-3.0). Its source code is available at
https://github.com/strukturag/libde265 and from the npm package tarball.

Source offer: on request, the complete corresponding source code of the
vendored libde265 artifact is provided. Written offer: vigilkit project
maintainers (see https://github.com/vigilkit/vigilkit).

Re-linkability: the libde265 WASM artifact is a physically isolated module
loaded at runtime by the loadLibde265() loader; it is not linked into this
package's JavaScript. Any build of libde265 exposing the same ESM API
(default async factory returning a Module with a `Decoder` class) can be
substituted by replacing the vendored artifact, and the package's
decode/encode logic does not depend on any specific libde265 version.

The Apache-2.0 license applies only to the glue code written by vigilkit;
it does not apply to the libde265 artifact itself.
